{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786504429,"nonce":"3PJ0a3YkdZGG7YsXPWnrbrudxu4=","title":"`lintreach` counts only the last hop of `\u0026x.A.B` as a write, and six of its own false positives were baselined as real debt","was":"**What is wrong.** `lintreach` treats `\u0026o.Alerts.Firing` as a write of `Firing` and a **read** of `Alerts`. Since `pgx` row scans are the tree's main way of filling a nested struct, any field whose only writer is a two-level `rows.Scan(\u0026x.A.B)` reads as never-written. Six such findings are sitting in `tools/lintreach/baseline.txt`, recorded as real debt, in a class the tool's own doc-comment claims cannot exist and in a file that explicitly forbids using it this way."}]}